        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f49fb96c9ffeAhQ2wArCq1yKm9\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough investigation. Here is the full report.\n\n---\n\n# Attachment and file-storage primitives in A2E Suite (twenty-server)\n\n## 0. Headline finding for the chat feature\n\nAn app object like `chatMessage` **already has an auto-provisioned polymorphic attachment surface**. When any object metadata is created, the engine provisions four default system relations, including one to the standard `attachment` object (`DEFAULT_RELATIONS_OBJECTS_STANDARD_IDS`). For a source object named `chatMessage` this yields:\n\n- forward `RELATION` field `attachments` on `chatMessage` (ONE_TO_MANY → `attachment`)\n- reverse `MORPH_RELATION` field `targetChatMessage` on `attachment`, join column `targetChatMessageId`, sharing the engine-pinned morph id `20202020-f634-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c69`\n- an engine-owned index on the reverse join column\n\nSo the chat feature does **not** need to declare an attachment field or a chat-owned file table; it should create `attachment` records with `targetChatMessageId` set (or use the `attachments` relation), exactly as the native Files activity does for tasks/notes/etc. Details and paths below.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The `Attachment` standard object\n\n### Workspace entity (TypeScript source of truth)\n`packages/twenty-server/src/modules/attachment/standard-objects/attachment.workspace-entity.ts` (46 lines)\n\n```ts\nexport class AttachmentWorkspaceEntity extends BaseWorkspaceEntity {           // :16\n  /** @deprecated Use `file[0].label` field instead */\n  name: string | null;                                                          // :18\n  file: FileOutput[] | null;                                                    // :19\n  /** @deprecated Use `file[0].fileId` field instead */\n  fullPath: string | null;                                                      // :21\n  /** @deprecated Use `fileCategory` field instead */\n  type: string | null;                                                          // :23\n  /** @deprecated Use `file[0].extension` field instead */\n  fileCategory: string;                                                         // :25\n  createdBy: ActorMetadata;                                                     // :26\n  updatedBy: ActorMetadata;                                                     // :27\n  /** @deprecated */\n  author: EntityRelation<WorkspaceMemberWorkspaceEntity> | null;                // :29\n  authorId: string | null;                                                      // :30\n  targetTask: EntityRelation<TaskWorkspaceEntity> | null;                       // :31\n  targetTaskId: string | null;                                                  // :32\n  targetNote / targetNoteId                                                     // :33-34\n  targetPerson / targetPersonId                                                 // :35-36\n  targetCompany / targetCompanyId                                               // :37-38\n  targetOpportunity / targetOpportunityId                                       // :39-40\n  targetDashboard / targetDashboardId                                           // :41-42\n  targetWorkflow / targetWorkflowId                                             // :43-44\n  custom: EntityRelation<CustomWorkspaceEntity>;                                // :45\n}\n```\n\nNotes:\n- The class lists only the seven standard morph targets plus a generic `custom`. App-object targets (e.g. `targetChatMessage`) are **runtime metadata**, not in this class.\n- `file` is the modern FILES backing field; `name`, `fullPath`, `type`, `fileCategory` are deprecated.\n\n### Field metadata (what actually exists in a workspace)\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-attachment-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` (653 lines)\n\n- `name` TEXT, nullable, UI-non-editable — lines 134-157\n- `file` **FILES**, `settings: { maxNumberOfValues: 1 }`, nullable — lines 158-184\n- `fullPath` TEXT (deprecated) — lines 186-210\n- `fileCategory` SELECT (deprecated), options `ARCHIVE/AUDIO/IMAGE/PRESENTATION/SPREADSHEET/TEXT_DOCUMENT/VIDEO/OTHER` — lines 212-311\n- `createdBy`/`updatedBy` ACTOR — lines 312-371\n- `position` POSITION — lines 372-396\n- `searchVector` TS_VECTOR — lines 397-420\n- Seven `MORPH_RELATION` targets — lines 422-652:\n  - `targetTask` join `targetTaskId`, `SET_NULL` (line 447)\n  - `targetNote` join `targetNoteId`, `SET_NULL` (line 480)\n  - `targetPerson`, `targetCompany`, `targetOpportunity`, `targetDashboard`, `targetWorkflow` all `CASCADE`\n  - every one sets `morphId: STANDARD_OBJECTS.attachment.morphIds.targetMorphId.morphId`, `targetFieldName: 'attachments'`, `isSystemSideEffect: true`\n\n### Morph id + shared constants\n`packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts:22-28`\n```ts\nattachment: {\n  universalIdentifier: STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.attachment,\n  fields: STANDARD_OBJECT_FIELDS.attachment,\n  morphIds: { targetMorphId: { morphId: '20202020-f634-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c69' } },\n  indexes: { ... }\n}\n```\n\n### File value type\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/common/common-args-processors/data-arg-processor/types/file-item.type.ts`\n```ts\nexport type FileInput  = { fileId: string; label: string };                  // :1\nexport type FileOutput = FileInput & { extension: string };                  // :6\nexport type SignedFileOutput = FileOutput & { url: string };                 // :10\n```\n\n### Front-end mirror\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/files/types/Attachment.ts` — `Attachment` type with `file: FieldFilesValue[] | null`, all `target*Id`, deprecated `fullPath`/`fileCategory`, `createdBy`. The `target*Id` naming is derived by `getActivityTargetObjectFieldIdName` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/utils/getActivityTargetObjectFieldIdName.ts:8`) as `` `target${capitalize(nameSingular)}Id` `` — for chat that is `targetChatMessageId`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. How attachments are linked to records\n\n### Model: one shared polymorphic morph (not per-object join tables)\nAll targets share a single `morphId`. The standard explicit targets are declared in `compute-attachment-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` (lines 422-652). Each target object owns the inverse `attachments` relation, e.g. `compute-person-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:576`, `compute-company-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:573`, `compute-task-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:383`, `compute-note-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:312`, `compute-dashboard-...:316`, `compute-workflow-...:485`, `compute-opportunity-...:566`.\n\n### Auto-provisioning for EVERY new object (key mechanism)\n`packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/default-relations-object-standard-ids.constant.ts`\n```ts\nexport const DEFAULT_RELATIONS_OBJECTS_STANDARD_IDS = [\n  'timelineActivity', 'attachment', 'noteTarget', 'taskTarget',\n] as const;\n```\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/metadata-side-effect/handlers/object-metadata/services/object-system-relations-on-create-side-effect-handler.service.ts` (114 lines):\n- On `objectMetadata` create, for each default relation object it emits a forward field on the new object and a reverse morph field on the standard object — lines 48-113.\n- The forward field name is the target object's `namePlural` (= `attachments`), reverse is `target<SourceSingular>` (e.g. `targetChatMessage`) — see `build-system-relation-flat-field-metadatas-for-object.util.ts:56-63`.\n- The builder `buildSystemRelationFlatFieldMetadatasForObject` (lines 45-124) uses `MORPH_ID_BY_STANDARD_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR.attachment` (line 25) and `STANDARD_RELATION_FIELD_PROPERTIES_BY_RELATION_OBJECT.attachment` = label `Attachments`, icon `IconPaperclip` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/object-metadata/constants/standard-relation-field-properties.constant.ts:15-18`).\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/object-metadata/utils/build-system-relation-flat-field-metadatas-for-object.util.ts:74-114` computes deterministic name-free universal identifiers via `getSystemRelationFieldUniversalIdentifier`, and calls `generateMorphOrRelationFlatFieldMetadataPair` with `targetFlatFieldMetadataType: FieldMetadataType.MORPH_RELATION`, `isSystemSideEffect: true` (lines 89-114).\n\n**Coverage proof:** `packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/successful-sync-application-workspace-migration.integration-spec.ts:235-314` asserts, for an app object (`TEST_APP_ID`/`TEST_OBJECT`), that the engine creates:\n- forward field named after the standard object's plural, `FieldMetadataType.RELATION`, `isSystemSideEffect: true` (lines 258-275)\n- reverse `targetTicket` `MORPH_RELATION` with the pinned `morphId` and `joinColumnName: 'targetTicketId'` (lines 277-299)\n- the reverse join-column index (lines 301-314)\n\nThe `custom.workspace-entity.ts:24` (`attachments: AttachmentWorkspaceEntity[]`) mirrors this for legacy custom objects.\n\n### Where attachments are actually created (native upload path)\nThe actual \"create the attachment row for a target\" logic is **client-side** for the native Files activity:\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/files/hooks/useUploadAttachmentFile.tsx:28-67`\n1. `directUploadFile(file, { fileFolder: FileFolder.FilesField, fieldMetadataId: attachment.file field id })` — line 37-40\n2. resolve target FK name via `getActivityTargetObjectFieldIdName` — lines 46-48\n3. `createOneAttachment({ name, [targetFieldIdName]: target.id, file: [{ fileId, label }] })` — lines 50-61\n\nRead path: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/files/hooks/useAttachments.tsx:6-27` queries the `attachment` object filtered by `target<Object>Id`.\n\n### Server-side copy-into-FILES-field (when a record is written with a FILES value)\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/tool-provider/services/record-files-resolver.service.ts:34-139`\n- `resolveRecordsInput({ objectNameSingular, records, workspaceId }): Promise<{ records, notes }>`\n- For each FILES field on the object, it finds copyable uploaded file ids (`isCopyableFilesFieldSourcePath`) and calls `filesFieldService.copyFileIntoFilesField(...)` (lines 95-107), substituting new ids.\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file/files-field/services/files-field.service.ts:114-194`\n- `copyFileIntoFilesField({ fileId, workspaceId, fieldMetadataId }): Promise<FileEntity>` — copies storage object and inserts a `FileEntity` (attributes to the field's owning application, lines 145-193).\n- `uploadFile({ file, filename, workspaceId, fieldMetadataId?, fieldMetadataUniversalIdentifier? }): Promise<FileWithSignedUrlDTO>` — lines 42-112.\n\nCopyable source folders (attribution-aware): `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/tool-provider/constants/files-field-copyable-source-folders.constant.ts` currently only `[FileFolder.AgentChat]`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. File-storage module\n\nRoot: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file-storage/`\n\n### Folder / domain enums\n`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/FileFolder.ts`\n```ts\nexport enum FileFolder {\n  CorePicture = 'core-picture',\n  AgentChat = 'agent-chat',        // existing AI-chat folder\n  BuiltLogicFunction = 'built-logic-function',\n  BuiltFrontComponent = 'built-front-component',\n  PublicAsset = 'public-asset',\n  Source = 'source',\n  FilesField = 'files-field',      // FILES fields / attachments\n  Dependencies = 'dependencies',\n  Workflow = 'workflow',\n  EmailAttachment = 'email-attachment',\n  EmailImage = 'email-image',\n  AppTarball = 'app-tarball',\n  GeneratedSdkClient = 'generated-sdk-client',\n  Dpa = 'dpa',\n}\n```\n\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file-storage/interfaces/file-storage.interface.ts`\n```ts\nexport enum StorageDriverType { S_3 = 'S_3', LOCAL = 'LOCAL' }   // :1-4\n```\n\nPer-folder MIME/cache policy: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file/interfaces/file-folder.interface.ts:27-98` (`fileFolderConfigs: Record<FileFolder, FileFolderConfig>`; `AgentChat` at lines 33-37; `FilesField` at lines 58-62). Also registers the GraphQL enum at lines 6-8.\n\n### Services / drivers\n- `file-storage.service.ts` (636 lines) — the central service. `ResourceIdentifier` type at lines 31-36: `{ workspaceId, applicationUniversalIdentifier, fileFolder: FileFolder, resourcePath }`.\n  - `writeFile({ sourceFile, fileFolder, applicationUniversalIdentifier, applicationId?, workspaceId, resourcePath, fileId?, settings, queryRunner? }): Promise<FileEntity>` — lines 198-264\n  - `createPendingFile({ fileFolder, applicationUniversalIdentifier, applicationId?, workspaceId, resourcePath, fileId, size, mimeType, settings }): Promise<FileEntity>` — lines 269-313\n  - `getPresignedUploadUrl(...): Promise<string | null>` — lines 342-359\n  - `getPresignedUrl`, `readFile`, `readFilePrefix`, `downloadFile`, `deleteFile`, `deleteFileObject`, `deleteByFileId`, `copy({from,to})`, `move({from,to,ifMatchChecksum?})`, `checkFileExists`, `deleteFolder`, `deleteApplicationFilesFromStorage` — lines 361-635\n  - Storage path layout: `${workspaceId}/${applicationUniversalIdentifier}/${fileFolder}/${resourcePath}` (lines 118-145), validated by `validate-storage-path-is-within-workspace-or-throw.util.ts`.\n- `file-storage-driver.factory.ts` — driver selection (`StorageDriverType`).\n- Drivers: `drivers/s3.driver.ts`, `drivers/local.driver.ts`, `drivers/validated-storage.driver.ts`, interface `drivers/interfaces/storage-driver.interface.ts`.\n- Folder path safety: `utils/validate-file-path.util.ts`, `validate-folder-path.util.ts`, `validate-safe-relative-path.util.ts`, `is-safe-relative-path.util.ts`, `assert-storage-path-is-safe.util.ts`, `has-allowed-extension.util.ts`, `prepare-file-for-storage-or-throw.util.ts`.\n- Constants: `constants/allowed-extensions-by-application-file-folder.constant.ts`, `server-file-storage-prefix.constant.ts`, `s3-client-timeouts.constant.ts`.\n\n### File record (native attribution + lifecycle)\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file/entities/file.entity.ts` (127 lines)\n- `id`, `workspaceId`, `applicationId` (line 67, `RESTRICT` FK to `ApplicationEntity` line 70-74), `applicationRegistrationId` (line 79-87), `path`, `size`, `createdAt/updatedAt/deletedAt`, `isStaticAsset`, `settings: FileSettings`, `mimeType`, `status: FileStatus` (PENDING/UPLOADED).\n- Uniques on `(workspaceId, applicationId, path)` and `(applicationRegistrationId, path)` — lines 44-52.\n\n### Upload orchestration (`file` core module)\n`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/file/file-upload/services/file-upload.service.ts`\n- `DIRECT_UPLOAD_FILE_FOLDERS = [FilesField, Workflow, EmailAttachment, AgentChat, EmailImage]` — lines 41-47\n- `createFileUpload({ workspaceId, filename, size, fileFolder, fieldMetadataId?, fieldMetadataUniversalIdentifier? }): Promise<FileUploadTargetDTO>` — lines 67-156\n- `receiveFileStream(...)` — lines 158-245\n- `completeFileUpload({ workspaceId, fileId }): Promise<FileWithSignedUrlDTO>` — lines 247-328\n- For `FilesField`, upload location resolves the **field's owning application** (lines 346-379): `applicationUniversalIdentifier = fieldMetadata.applicationId app`, `resourcePath = ${fieldMetadata.universalIdentifier}/${name}`.\n- `file-upload-target.service.ts` — `buildUploadTarget`, `createUploadTargetsBatch`, presigned vs token upload.\n- `file-upload-completion.service.ts` — MIME sniff, SVG sanitize, promote pending → final, set `UPLOADED`.\n- GraphQL resolver: `file-upload/resolvers/file-upload.resolver.ts`; controller `file-upload/controllers/file-upload.controller.ts`.\n- URL signing: `file/file-url/file-url.service.ts`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. \"sourceApp\" / source attribution\n\nThere is **no `sourceApp` or `source_app` field on `attachment` in-tree today.** A repo-wide grep finds `sourceApp` only under `Inspiration apps (bureaubilan)/` (the reference apps). Confirmed by the P6 spike report:\n\n`docs/plan/phases/phase-06-report.md:135-136`\n> `sourceApp`/`starred`/`description` on `attachment` do not exist yet (P6.1 bullet 3 remains `[ ]`).\n\nand `docs/plan/phases/phase-06-report.md:97-98` (view filtering by `sourceApp` is the plan), plus PLAN.md:\n- `PLAN.md:988-989`: \"Attachment extensions: folderId, starred, sourceApp (attribution like Bureau `sourceApp`), description\" — still unchecked.\n- `PLAN.md:297-299`: \"File fields use attachment/file-storage primitives; source-app attribution is not ownership or permission.\"\n- `docs/plan/02-reference-analysis.md:72` (R08 Files) describes the external Bureau/Bilan source-app labels that motivated this; R08 is a reference row, not implemented here.\n\nWhat exists natively as attribution:\n- Every `FileEntity` row carries `applicationId` (and `applicationRegistrationId`), i.e. the **Application that owns the bytes** — `file.entity.ts:67-87`.\n- Storage path is namespaced by application: `${workspaceId}/${applicationUniversalIdentifier}/${fileFolder}/...` — `file-storage.service.ts:118-145`.\n- When uploading into a FILES field, the file is attributed to the application that owns that field — `file-upload.service.ts:346-379`, `files-field.service.ts:84-95`.\n- The variable names `sourceApplication`/`destinationApplication` in `files-field.service.ts:150-180` are about copy source/destination, not a metadata field.\n- `createdBy`/`updatedBy` ACTOR fields on `attachment` are the record-level actor attribution (`compute-attachment-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:312-371`).\n\nSo for chat, \"source attribution\" today = the owning application captured on the `FileEntity`, and the morph target (`targetChatMessageId`) on the `attachment` row; the explicit `sourceApp` label is a planned additive attachment field (P6.1), not an existing primitive.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Tests\n\n### Attachment-specific\n- Integration GraphQL CRUD: `packages/twenty-server/test/integration/graphql/suites/object-generated/attachments.integration-spec.ts` (queries `name`, `fullPath`, `target*Id`; note it still references generated `targetPetId`/`targetSurveyResultId` from other test objects).\n- No dedicated unit tests under `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/attachment` (only the entity file exists); the module has no services/resolvers.\n- Upgrade-command specs referencing attachment timeline types: `.../upgrade-version-command/2-34/__tests__/2-34-workspace-command-1787471738599-add-attachment-timeline-activity-types.command.spec.ts`, `.../2-35/__tests__/2-35-workspace-command-1787561579075-repair-attachment-timeline-activity-types.command.spec.ts`.\n- Object-metadata mock: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-object-metadata/__mocks__/attachment-flat-object.mock.ts`.\n- Auto-provisioning of the `attachment` morph for app/custom objects: `test/integration/metadata/suites/application/successful-sync-application-workspace-migration.integration-spec.ts:235-314` (see section 2).\n\n### File upload / FILES field\n- `test/integration/graphql/suites/file-upload/direct-file-upload.integration-spec.ts` (332 lines; `createFileUpload`/`completeFileUpload`/`deleteFile`).\n- `test/integration/graphql/suites/files-field/files-field-download.integration-spec.ts`\n- `test/integration/graphql/suites/files-field/files-field-sync.integration-spec.ts`\n- Input validation: `test/integration/graphql/suites/inputs-validation/create-validation/files-field-create-input-validation.integration-spec.ts` (+ snapshot) and `.../filter-validation/files-field-filter-input-validation.integration-spec.ts`.\n- Unit: `file/files-field/services/__tests__/files-field.service.copy-file-into-files-field.spec.ts`; `file/file-upload/services/__tests__/file-upload-completion.service.spec.ts`; `.../file-upload.service.create-file-upload.spec.ts`; `.../build-pending-upload-resource-path.util.spec.ts`; `file/controllers/file.controller.spec.ts`; and many `file/utils/__tests__/*` and `file-storage/utils/__tests__/*` specs.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The `a2e-chat` app\n\nRoot: `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/` (app package name `a2e-chat`, version 0.1.0, `twenty-sdk`/`twenty-client-sdk` 2.31.0 — `package.json`).\n\n### Application declaration\n`src/application.config.ts` — `defineApplication`, `APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER = 'e2dce399-87f1-4548-b307-5f368b4d5dd4'`, displayName \"A2E Chat\".\n\n### Objects (`src/objects/`)\nAll five defined with `defineObject` from `twenty-sdk/define`, French labels, UUID block `c31c*`:\n\n| File | singular/plural | key fields |\n|---|---|---|\n| `chat-channel.object.ts` | `chatChannel`/`chatChannels` | `name`, `kind` (WORKSPACE/PROJECT/CUSTOM), `visibility` (PUBLIC/PRIVATE), `topic`, `postingRoles`; relations `messages`, `members`, `readCursors` |\n| `chat-channel-member.object.ts` | `chatChannelMember`/`chatChannelMembers` | `memberRole` (OWNER/MEMBER), `joinedAt`; `channel`, `workspaceMember` |\n| `chat-message.object.ts` | `chatMessage`/`chatMessages` | `body` (TEXT, label id), `editedAt`; `channel` (M2O CASCADE), `author` (M2O SET_NULL), `threadParent`/`threadReplies` (self), `reactions`, `readCursors` |\n| `chat-reaction.object.ts` | `chatReaction`/`chatReactions` | `emoji`; `message` (CASCADE), `workspaceMember` (CASCADE) |\n| `chat-read-cursor.object.ts` | `chatReadCursor`/`chatReadCursors` | `lastReadAt`; `channel`, `workspaceMember`, `lastReadMessage` |\n\n**`chatMessage` has no explicit attachment field or FILES field** (`src/objects/chat-message.object.ts:29-126`). A grep for \"attach\" inside `src/` only matches comments and \"rattaché\" text. The only relation-style declaration to external objects is `author` → `workspaceMember` (lines 62-77), with the inverse declared separately in `src/fields/workspace-member-messages.field.ts` as `chatMessages`.\n\n### Page layout (the attachment intent)\n`src/page-layouts/chat-message.page-layout.ts:5-32`\n```\n// Message record page: fields + the native files widget. Attachments use the\n// shared attachment/file-storage primitives (P5.1 attachments leg), never a\n// chat-owned file table.\n```\nTabs: `Accueil` with widgets `FIELDS` and `FILES` (`type: 'FILES'`, `configuration: { configurationType: 'FILES' }`) — lines 20-33. The record page also has a `RECORD_PAGE` type.\n\nViews: `src/views/all-channels.view.ts`, `all-channel-members.view.ts`, `all-messages.view.ts` (fields `body`, `channel`, `author`, `editedAt`; unsorted by design — `all-messages.view.ts:9-58`).\n\nFields on standard objects: `src/fields/workspace-member-channel-memberships.field.ts`, `workspace-member-messages.field.ts`, `workspace-member-reactions.field.ts`, `workspace-member-read-cursors.field.ts`.\n\nSupporting: `src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts` (all UUIDs, additive-only law, `OBJECT_IDS`, `RELATION_IDS`, `LABEL_IDENTIFIER_IDS`, etc.), `src/constants/field-vocabulary.ts` (select options, `oneToMany`, `manyToOne`, re-exports `FieldType`), `src/lib/message-body.ts`, `src/lib/channel-membership.ts`, `src/lib/starter-channels.ts`, `src/logic-functions/post-install.ts` + `handlers/starter-channels-handler.ts`, `src/front-components/*`, `src/command-menu-items/*`, `src/navigation-menu-items/channels.navigation-menu-item.ts`, `src/roles/default-function.role.ts` (canDestroy false).\n\n### Constraints from the manifest integrity test\n`src/lib/__tests__/chat-object-integrity.test.ts` (598 lines) walks the whole manifest: exactly five objects (lines 266-286), no duplicate universal identifiers (288-364), every relation target resolves (366-397), every relation is a symmetric M2O/O2M pair (399-461), views/layouts/roles resolve, and every `RELATION_IDS` entry is used exactly once (577-598). Adding an attachment relation to `chatMessage` would need a new universal identifier here.\n\n### SDK support for the two possible chat-attachment approaches\n- The manifest type supports `MORPH_RELATION` fields with an explicit `morphId` on any object (including standard objects): `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/fieldManifestType.ts:48-64`.\n- The SDK exposes `FieldType.FILES` and validates FILES fields: `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/fields/validate-fields.ts:42-43`, `.../validate-fields.ts:214-228`.\n- Front components can upload directly to a FILES field: `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/front-component/globals/frontComponentHostCommunicationApi.ts:123-147` (`UploadFileParams.fieldMetadataId`, comment lines 131-134: uploads must target a FILES field or strand a temporary orphan).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Concrete takeaways for a chat message attachment feature\n\n1. Reuse the single `attachment` morph id `20202020-f634-435d-ab8d-e1168b375c69`; do not create parallel storage.\n2. `chatMessage.attachments` and `attachment.targetChatMessage` are expected to already exist automatically after install (object-create side-effect handler; see section 2 and the app-sync integration test). Verify at install time, since the TypeScript `AttachmentWorkspaceEntity` does not enumerate it.\n3. The upload path to reuse is FILES-field direct upload: `createFileUpload`/`completeFileUpload` with `fileFolder: FileFolder.FilesField` and a `fieldMetadataId` (or `FileFolder.AgentChat` for AI-chat style uploads), then create an `attachment` row pointing at the target via `targetChatMessageId` with `file: [{ fileId, label }]` — mirroring `useUploadAttachmentFile.tsx:28-67`.\n4. Source attribution today is `FileEntity.applicationId` + the storage path namespace and the morph target; an explicit `sourceApp` attachment field does not exist (planned P6.1, PLAN.md:988).\n5. Reuse existing tests as templates: `attachments.integration-spec.ts`, `files-field-sync.integration-spec.ts`, `files-field-download.integration-spec.ts`, `direct-file-upload.integration-spec.ts`, and the app manifest integrity test pattern.\n\nNo code was written or modified during this investigation.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
